  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">USAID Rule of Law/Anti-Corruption Activity in the Kyrgyz Republic, Ukuk Bulagy</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Kyrgyz Republic):  USAID&apos;s Rule-of-Law and Anti-Corruption Activity, known as &quot;Ukuk Bulagy,&quot; will continue to strengthen the transparency and accountability of the judiciary and other key government institutions by supporting the following four objectives: 1) Strengthen the judiciary as a core pillar of the governance and rule of law architecture; 2) Strengthen justice and legal services to address legal problems, resolve disputes, and protect fundamental rights and thus close the justice gap; 3) Strengthen the connection between the judiciary and society by ensuring that the systems and services are more responsive to the population as a whole and equipped to address the legal problems and justice needs of the communities and businesses they are mandated to service; and, 4) Engage select executive institutions and parliament to strengthen open government policies and the delivery of services across sectors in a more transparent, accountable, and citizen-responsive manner. In addition, by improving service delivery and reducing everyday corruption, the activity strengthens Kyrgyz democratic institutions and contributes to rebuilding the Kyrgyz Republic&apos;s constituency for democracy. This activity will support ICS objective 3.1: A culture of respect for rule of law with reduced corruption. USAID&apos;s contribution to meeting the $12,000,000 DRG directive through this IM is $1,915,000. The FY 2022 Operating Unit TIP directive is $1,000,000. USAID&apos;s contribution to meeting the TIP directive through this IM is $80,000.</narrative>
  </description>
